  "solution": {
    "text": "We know that voltage amplification is given by,<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>",
